A||N||5||Dean||Still Runs Rough When Cold||||1||
Z||000000||Dean||12-06-2001||07:58 AM||||1986, 2.5L. The car runs rough when just started from cold, and slightly rough when not fully warmed up. I've replaced the Idle Air Control, O2 sensor, plugs, wires, distributor, set the timing, checked for vacuum leaks, etc. Compression is at 180 in each cylinder with no significant leakdown.<P>I'm still assuming this is a sensor somewhere going wrong. The manual shows no temp sensor hooked to the computer that would do this other than the above units which are freshly replaced. <P>The car went into the shop for diagnostics which showed the IAC and the O2 sensor, but those were replaced with little change.<P>Any help appreciated.||||reg||1
Z||000001||ka4nkf||12-07-2001||02:01 AM||||I am not to much on the four cylinder, and it looks like you have changed everything that I could think of. you might check the thermo vac on the air cleaner and see if it is working. wish I could help more.||||reg||1
Z||000002||johnt671||12-07-2001||08:10 AM||||Try changing the temp. sensor for the computer.  Not the sending unit for the temp gauge.  I've read that if this sensor fails the computer thinks it's -30 degrees.  I'm basing this on your statement on you saying it also runs bad when warmed up.  Try pulling a spark plug and see if it is black or wet. This would show the car running rich. If it is then my guess is the temp sensor.  ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Dean||12-07-2001||08:22 AM||||Where is the temp sensor for the computer located? My manual is poor and doesn't tell me where it is on the engine.<P>Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000004||reddog||12-07-2001||11:36 PM||||Coolant temp sensor and thermostat????? Maybe!!!!!!!<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Picturenew_sig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||fotofrank||12-08-2001||01:16 AM||||T think it is on or at the coolant filler neck to the left of the engine. There are two temp sensors in the car the one for the temp gauge is inthe head on the left side of the head and the other, I belive, is on or at the coolant filler neck. My '84 Duke is a little slow or rough when accellerating from a dead stop when cold and is OK when worm. Above about 1500 RPM or so the engine runs fine all the time<P>------------------<BR>Peace and Happiness<BR>Frank and his fotoflash, an '84 SE||||reg||10
